    "issue_alignment": "In the JSON encoding module (src/ua_types_encoding_json.c), Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject frees the allocation stored in dst->data when the inner body decode fails, but never clears the pointer or the variant type. UA_decodeJson's generic error cleanup (UA_deleteMembers -> UA_Variant_clear -> UA_Array_delete) then frees the same memory again, yielding a double-free. The PoC triggers this via {\"Type\":22,\"Body\":{\"TypeId\":{\"Id\":6},\"Body\":\"abc\"}}: Type 22 (ExtensionObject) selects the unwrap path, TypeId 6 (Int32) causes an allocation, and the malformed non-primitive Body makes the inner decode fail so the dangling pointer is freed twice."
